**July 2022:  The following instructions are subject to review**

If you currently buy a device it probably comes with the software-version 3.xx which has a different flash layout ("OS1" starts at 0x260000 instead of 0x160000). So you first have to flash an older version via TFTP, then use [[https://github.com/acecilia/OpenWRTInvasion|OpenWRTInvasion]] to get a root-shell and flash OpenWrt.

  - Download [[https://bigota.miwifi.com/xiaoqiang/rom/r4ac/miwifi_r4ac_all_c4b35_2.18.28.bin|miwifi_r4ac_all_c4b35_2.18.28.bin]], rename it to ''test.bin'' and put it in the root-folder of your TFTP-Server. Set a static IP-address and start a DHCP-Server. Now plug in the router while holding the reset button until the amber LED starts flashing. The router will now download and flash the ''test.bin''-file. Restart the router once the LED starts flashing blue.
  - Once the router finished booting, go to [[http://192.168.31.1/]] and set up the router
  - Use [[https://github.com/acecilia/OpenWRTInvasion|OpenWRTInvasion]] to get a root-shell
  - Download the openwrt-**<color #ed1c24>sysupgrade</color>**-image to ''/tmp'' and write it to the flash with ''mtd -r write <image> OS1''

